==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|Swiss Standard German}} {{l/de|stossen}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|stōzan}} from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*stautaną}}. Akin to {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|stauta}} and {{m|non|steyta}} (whence {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|støde}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌿𐍄𐌰𐌽}}. Non-Germanic cognates include {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|tundo}}. Compare {{etyl|sa|-}} {{m|sa|तुदति||tr=tudati|to strike, goad}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃtoːsən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-stoßen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=7|stößt|stieß|gestoßen}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=de}} to [[push]]; to [[shove]]; to [[thrust]]
# {{context|transitive|or|reflexive|lang=de}} to [[bump]]; to [[knock]]; to [[strike]]; to [[hurt]]
# {{context|reflexive|figuratively|with ''[[an#German|an]]''|lang=de}} to [[take exception]] (to something)
# {{context|intransitive|lang=de}} to [[jolt]]; to [[kick]]; to [[thrust]]

